<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Francisville, Louisiana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. Francisville is a small town on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a> in West Feliciana Parish, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>. In 1810 it served as the capital of the short-lived Republic of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, proclaimed by Anglo-American settlers against Spanish rule. The town is known for its antebellum plantation houses.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-francisville-louisiana.jpg" alt="St. Francisville, Louisiana" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hank5720 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Butlergreen_woodpecker.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
